meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: "Air Quality Life Index (AQLI)"
    description: |-
      The Air Quality Life Index (AQLI) by the Energy Policy Institute at the University of Chicago showcases the potential for life expectancy gains if air pollution levels were reduced. Fine particle pollution (PM2.5) shortens people's lives when they breathe them in, the AQLI projects how many more years people could live if pollution was reduced to meet the World Health Organization's guidelines (an annual exposure of 5 µg/m3). Using global, satellite-derived data, the AQLI provides a detailed picture of air pollution levels and their health impact around the world, tracking changes from 1998 to 2022. This information can be used to inform policies and actions that aim to improve air quality and public health.
    date_published: "2026-03-29"
    title_snapshot: "Air Quality Life Index (AQLI) - Subnational data at GADM level 2 (counties, districts, municipalities)"
    description_snapshot: |-
      AQLI data at GADM level 2 — smaller areas within GADM level 1 regions, such as counties, districts, or municipalities. The ZIP contains the data in both wide and narrow (long) table formats. Columns provide, by year (1998–2023), the annual average PM2.5 concentration (µg/m3, `pm` prefix), the potential gain in life expectancy if the WHO guideline of 5 µg/m3 were met (`who` prefix, in years), and the potential gain if the country's national standard were met (`nat` prefix, in years), along with each area's population and national PM2.5 standard. Some countries lack GADM level 2 region names, so their most granular available data is at GADM level 1 or level 0.

    # Citation
    producer: "Energy Policy Institute at the University of Chicago (EPIC)"
    citation_full: |-
      Air Quality Life Index (AQLI) by the Energy Policy Institute at the University of Chicago (https://aqli.epic.uchicago.edu/) (2024)
    attribution_short: "AQLI"

    # Files
    url_main: https://aqli.epic.uchicago.edu/
    # NOTE: the 2026 release also ships gadm0_aqli.zip (country level, snapshotted as air_quality_life_index) and gadm1_aqli.zip (snapshotted as air_quality_life_index_gadm1), plus a Readme.md — not snapshotted (2026-09-07)
    url_download: https://github.com/aqli-epic/aqli-update/raw/main/AQLI%20Annual%20Update%202026%20data/gadm2_aqli.zip
    date_accessed: '2026-09-07'

